# apify push skips what .gitignore lists, and .gitignore lists src/shield/ (the copy of shield/ bundle.sh writes, kept
# out of git), so without this the build fails with ModuleNotFoundError. A "!" line here force-includes files again
# even when git ignores them (apify-cli getActorLocalFilePaths; an older apify-cli without .actorignore support skips
# them: update it). Run sh bundle.sh before apify push.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
!src/shield/**/*.py
